gy and  astronomy were synonymous in other words  astrology was the best astronomy humans  had during this time it's true that  accurate observations of the stars and  planet  what we think of as astronomy was the  foundation of astrology and that's still  true about astrology today to some  degree but astrology and astronomy began  to split apart during the 17th and 18th  centuries as more modern versions of  science began developing and the  supernatural claims made by astrology  were challenged so astrology was  abandoned in the intellectual world and  astronomy has been firmly considered a  separate distinct discipline since the  late 18th century and this is worth  noting that the split between astrology  and astronomy happened upon the  emergence of the scientific method  that's not a coincidence but it sort of  makes sense that pre science humans  would think that the Stars were sending  the messages or influencing human  affairs think about the last time you  could see the Stars clearly it's  awe-inspiring ancient cultures that  didn't have natural explanations for  what they were seeing would  unsurprisingly invent their own  explanations humans are programmed to  make inferences about things they don't  understand so astrology is really just a  way of thinking that is left over from  outdated attempts at science but don't  get me wrong astrology can be very  intricate it can seem scientific enough  because tracking planets and  constellations is something that real  scientists do using complex equations  and charts and a ton of math and this is  why many people are tricked into  thinking astrology is science but I  could use formulas and math to track the  blades of grass in a park to make  predictions about the stock market the  formulas and math don't actually make it  meaningful  astrology believes the time of your  birth and the position of celestial  bodies at that time can determine your  personality strengths weaknesses  compatibility with people born at other  times and more who you should befriend  who you should date decisions you should  make in life and central to astrology  our horoscopes which make predictions  about people's behavior and destinies  based on where and when they were born  which determines what's known as their  Sun Sign  like virgo libra Scorpio Sagittarius we  see horoscopes all over the place  let's look at a random horoscope I found  I didn't cherry pick this this was the  first horoscope I found online quote  everyone looks to you for the answers  today but that doesn't rattle you at all  you're one cool customer and nothing is  going to get the better of you  maybe it's healthy confidence or a bit  of self delusion the reason for your  grace under pressure is irrelevant what  matters is that you'll be there for the  people who need you and your actions  will say everything that needs to be  said you could argue that what I just  read is how most people feel on most  days the whole point is its general  enough for parts to apply to anyone and  to seem relatable to anyone who reads it  on any random day there have been many  experiments where a roomful of people  get the same horoscope people with  different astrological signs and almost  everybody in the room says the horoscope  is accurate and relevant to their lives  people tend to rate claims about them as  accurate if they're vague enough and if  the person thinks that the claim was  tailored to them separating the  population into twelve signs that each  get their own horoscope gives this  illusion of a personally tailored claim  and the writers of horoscopes take  advantage of what's called self-serving  bias where people agree more in general  with flattering or positive descriptions  of themselves or their situation  horoscopes are rarely specific and they  almost never tell you about how horrible  your day is going to be or what a bad  person you are  even though bad days and bad people  obviously exist check out your own  